<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Lavra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">963</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Megisti Lavra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Lavra is the oldest and largest of the monasteries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, founded in 963 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athanasios-the-athonite">Athanasios the Athonite</a> with the support of the future Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a>. It turned Athos from a land of hermits into a community of organised monasteries and still ranks first among the twenty ruling monasteries. Its library holds thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-lavra.jpg" alt="Great Lavra" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aroche · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Megistis_Lavras_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
